---
// The network behind the hero of the home page (issue 81): a canvas that
// covers its section (which must be `relative` and carry
// `data-network-scope`), behind the content, with no size of its own, so
// nothing moves when it draws. It is decoration: hidden from assistive
// technology, never a target of the pointer, and not printed. Its color is
// the class `text-network`, which its script reads. The text that it
// keeps readable carries `data-network-quiet`. Without the script the canvas
// stays empty.
---

<canvas
    class='pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 h-full w-full text-network print:hidden'
    aria-hidden='true'
    data-network
></canvas>
<script>
    import { startNetworkLayers } from '../background/network-layer.ts'
    startNetworkLayers(document)
</script>
